  "sourceState": "Interface revision 2 declares the hlp.ui.use-can-show-master-detail dependency (ticket 154): the React docked-versus-modal gate is the capability policy itself (the panel calls useCanShowMasterDetail; the railCapable prop stays as the override seam), while the Blazor gate stays constant-bound to FormFactorQueries.MasterDetailRail pending a Blazor policy projection. The module still carries the legacy WorkspaceShell inspector region as a page-level selection-detail panel; no Shipyard source is copied. Both projections prove native, shared-conformance, and drawer-pattern dismissal gates. Interface revision 3 adds the drill-down levels from the design corpus (drilldown-model.md rows 1-3 and disclosure-model.md's subsection rule): facets are addressable count-bearing tabs, exactly one push carries a named back row, a second push is refused by absence and the only onward control is the declared Open as page action. One fixture, conformance/hlp.ui.detail-panel/drilldown-v1.json, is replayed by both projections.",
